    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d636">

                <pb facs="0547" n="431" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg431"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.124/233.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 128.</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-08-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 6, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt, of the Department’s telegraphic instruction of July 30 and to enclose
                    herewith a <pb facs="0548" n="432" xml:id="pg432"/> copy of my note No. 85 to
                    the Ecuadorian Foreign Office, which embodied the instruction above noted. The
                    matter has been referred to the Junta de Sanidad of Guayaquil, which under the
                    law must give its consent to the disbursement of funds for purposes of
                    sanitation.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rutherfurd Bingham.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d636-a1.xml" xpointer="d636-a1"/>
            </div>
